WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.380
Welcome to Grade 3 English, Unit
8: Numbers, Shapes, and Measurement.

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.080
Welcome to Unit 8!

3
00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:10.700
In this unit you will use English
to talk about maths in real life.

4
00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:14.660
You will count and name big
numbers, all the way up to a million.

5
00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:19.800
You will learn the words for addition,
subtraction, multiplication, and division.

6
00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:26.040
You will measure things around you — their size,
height, weight, and the distance between them —

7
00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:28.620
using words like meter and centimeter.

8
00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:32.240
You will also look for patterns and straight lines.

9
00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:37.250
Maths is everywhere: in the market, in
the kitchen, and on the way to the masjid.

10
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:44.640
By the end, you will be ready to solve a number puzzle,
just like Isaac and Hannah do in this unit's story.

11
00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:51.440
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

12
00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:57.840
By the end of this unit, you will be able
to read and say big numbers, up to a million.

13
00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:04.780
you will also use the maths words addition,
subtraction, multiplication, and division.

14
00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:09.660
you will also measure the size, height,
weight, and distance of things around you.

15
00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:12.660
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

16
00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:21.400
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
number, million, fact, pattern, straight, addition.

17
00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:27.380
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

18
00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:31.260
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

19
00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:37.400
The reading sequence includes Maths
Is Everywhere and A Pattern Poem.

20
00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:39.280
Read actively.

21
00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:45.040
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

22
00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:49.460
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

23
00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:54.500
The first language focus is Present Simple and Imperatives.

24
00:01:55.140 --> 00:02:01.740
The Present Simple tells about things that happen often or
facts that are always true, like “The sun rises in the east.”

25
00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:06.480
An imperative is a command or
instruction, like “Measure the height.”

26
00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:10.460
Both help us speak and write clearly, especially in maths.

27
00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:17.540
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

28
00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:22.640
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 — Measure and Tell.

29
00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:27.980
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

30
00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:32.020
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

31
00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:36.100
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

32
00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:37.800
You are ready to begin.

33
00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:44.600
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

34
00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:47.220
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

35
00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:53.020
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
